 of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-09-29T19:16:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75764, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "tls@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 25, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/75764/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/13/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-03-31T23:56:23Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-09-29T19:16:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 75774, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "tls@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 25, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/75774/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/14/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-03T20:50:45Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-09-29T19:16:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76411, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "tls@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 25, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/76411/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/111/", "/api/v1/doc/state/15/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-04T02:07:10Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-09-29T19:16:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 76439, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 25, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/76439/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/15/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-16T18:11:14Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-09-29T19:16:14Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 77903, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 25, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/77903/", "rev": "08", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-04-17T07:08:43Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-11-13T21:23:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 78144, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/78144/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/19/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-05-12T20:23:39Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-11-13T21:23:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 78252, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/78252/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-05-16T18:04:07Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-11-13T21:23:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 78740, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/78740/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/12/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-05-19T16:58:36Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-11-13T21:23:39Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 78938, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/78938/", "rev": "09", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/112/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/point/"], "time": "2015-05-28T19:38:22Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 78941, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/78941/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/9/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/point/"], "time": "2015-06-01T22:50:55Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 78947, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/78947/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/10/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-06-01T23:19:36Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79004, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/79004/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/10/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2015-06-01T23:49:54Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79006, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/79006/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/10/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/", "/api/v1/name/doctagname/iana/"], "time": "2015-06-01T23:49:54Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79277, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/79277/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/", "/api/v1/name/doctagname/iana/"], "time": "2015-06-02T18:59:27Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79603, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/79603/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/104/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/", "/api/v1/name/doctagname/iana/"], "time": "2015-06-08T18:37:15Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79698, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/79698/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/103/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/", "/api/v1/name/doctagname/iana/"], "time": "2015-06-16T18:25:14Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79767, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/79767/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/104/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/", "/api/v1/name/doctagname/iana/"], "time": "2015-06-18T08:09:00Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 79916, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.ad@ietf.org, tls-chairs@ietf.org, turners@ieca.com, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe.shepherd@ietf.org, draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe@ietf.org", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/79916/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/107/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2015-06-19T18:26:21Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 98690, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/98690/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/34/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:53:08Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 99831, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/99831/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/117/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:53:08Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 100685, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/100685/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/32/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:53:08Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 102797, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe", "note": "", "notify": "", "pages": 26, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/102797/", "rev": "10", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/turners@ieca.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/108/", "/api/v1/doc/state/115/", "/api/v1/doc/state/17/", "/api/v1/doc/state/25/", "/api/v1/doc/state/44/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": ["/api/v1/name/doctagname/ref/"], "time": "2015-10-14T20:53:08Z", "title": "Negotiated Finite Field Diffie-Hellman Ephemeral Parameters for TLS", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   Traditional finite-field-based Diffie-Hellman (DH) key exchange\n   during the TLS handshake suffers from a number of security,\n   interoperability, and efficiency shortcomings.  These shortcomings\n   arise from lack of clarity about which DH group parameters TLS\n   servers should offer and clients should accept.  This document offers\n   a solution to these shortcomings for compatible peers by using a\n   section of the TLS \"EC Named Curve Registry\" to establish common\n   finite-field DH parameters with known structure and a mechanism for\n   peers to negotiate support for these groups.\n\n   This draft updates TLS versions 1.0 [RFC2246], 1.1 [RFC4346], and 1.2\n   [RFC5246], as well as the TLS ECC extensions [RFC4492].\n", "ad": "/api/v1/person/person/19177/", "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-negotiated-ff-dhe/", "expires": "2015-12-03T23:50:55Z", "external_url": "", "gr